A1. Never found around a flapper. ~ CORSET
A7. A dumb-waiter never does this. ~ SPEAKS
A13. A city of ancient Palestine. ~ SAMARIA
A14. Many a good man missed the point this way. ~ PARRIED
A16. This fellow was the only man in the world for ie girl. ~ ADAM
A17. The apple of discontent. ~ GREEN
A19. Indian. (A combining form.) ~ INDO
A20. French verse. ~ VERS
A21. From this place. ~ HENCE
A22. You must do this before you hold hands. ~ DEAL
A23. A good place to be when it rains. ~ IN
A24. Right there. ~ AT
A25. This is smooth. ~ OILY
A27. Fifty-fifty in ancient Rome. ~ LL
A28. Where permanent waves are found. ~ OCEAN
A31. Better than any king. ~ ACE
A32. Girl's name. (A song hit of not so long ago.) ~ SONIA
A35. Something that couldn't be false. ~ REAL
A36. The end of a good cigar. ~ ASH
A37. To go up in the air again. ~ RESOAR
A38. Where good spirits come from. ~ VIALS
A40. The name of a country gentleman. ~ HIRAM
A41. An insect. ~ WEEVIL
A43. A swallow that does not fly. ~ SIP
A44. Just a lot of old jokes. ~ GAGS
A47. Relieved. ~ EASED
A48. Mike's boy friend. ~ IKE
A49. This is always at the foot. ~ PEDAL
A50. A painstaking gentleman (abbr.). ~ DR
A51. This is a bird. ~ ERNE
A53. This man is on top of The World (abbr.). ~ ED
A54. A part of New York that reaches out to sea. (Init.). ~ LI
A55. You're supposed to laugh at these. ~ GAGS
A58. "Oh, how I cry over you." ~ ONION
A60. Greedy. ~ AVID
A62. The color of unbleached linen. ~ ECRU
A63. What girls make up to go out. ~ MINDS
A64. A merrie old king. ~ COLE
A65. Flappers can't do this to their skirts any more. ~ SHORTEN
A67. People who can't do this puzzle. ~ DUMMIES
A69. A good drink for invalids. ~ EGGNOG
A70. To get out. ~ SECEDE

D1. An important part of jazz. ~ CADENCE
D2. An anti-prohibitionist of Old Persia. ~ OMAR
D3. These are woolly. ~ RAMS
D4. The old man (abbr.). ~ SR
D5. Ada, from Decadah. ~ EIGHT
D6. A leguminous plant. ~ TARE
D7. Good pocket lining. ~ SPECIE
D8. This is something to a door. ~ PANEL
D9. What they say when they don't know what to say. ~ ER
D10. Dry. (Like the U S in America.) ~ ARID
D11. Bovine animals. ~ KINE
D12. City in Missouri you've never heard of. ~ SEDALIA
D13. One who saves. ~ SAVIOR
D15. It takes cents to get this. ~ DOLLAR
D18. This fellow was older than Methuselah. (See Gen. v: 18.) ~ ENOCH
D24. The last of Susan. ~ AN
D26. A river in France. ~ YSER
D29. These are on the house. (Probably over your head.) ~ EAVES
D30. What tired business men are supposed to be in the daytime. ~ ALIVE
D31. Balaam's companion. ~ ASS
D33. An Indian. ~ OSAGE
D34. The wanderer. ~ NOMAD
D36. Everyone. ~ ALL
D37. A sad parting. ~ RIP
D39. An assistant. ~ AIDE
D40. To hasten. ~ HIE
D41. These get in where nothing else can. ~ WEDGES
D42. This hurts the best ear. ~ EARACHE
D43. There's good yarn in this. ~ SKEIN
D45. An ancient Roman province. ~ GALILEE
D46. Slips. ~ SLIDES
D48. Several of these in every baseball game. ~ INNING
D49. What you get on pay day (abbr.). ~ PD
D52. A famous porch climber. ~ ROMEO
D53. To follow as a consequence. ~ ENSUE
D56. The spirit of Christmas. ~ GROG
